From 4261d7bbee995c4ee08c1200bbbfa11d8568d6b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:40:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] configure: link libatomic only where atomics need it

The stdatomic check tried -latomic first and kept it whenever it
linked, so every build on a machine with libatomic installed named it
in each library's EXTRALIBS and pkg-config file, though on x86-64,
AArch64 and the other targets with native atomics nothing is taken
from it. A static consumer then carries a libatomic.so.1 dependency
it does not use, and a shared one a NEEDED entry (unless linked with
--as-needed).

Try without it first, and add it only when the atomics do not link
without it, which is what the comment above already said the -latomic
attempt was for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index 86a2437..a59d76f 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -7010,8 +7010,9 @@ check_headers asm/types.h
 # so we also check that atomics actually work here
 #
 # some configurations also require linking to libatomic, so try
-# both with -latomic and without
-for LATOMIC in "-latomic" ""; do
+# both without -latomic and with, in that order, so that a toolchain
+# that has libatomic but does not need it does not link it
+for LATOMIC in "" "-latomic"; do
     check_builtin stdatomic stdatomic.h                                \
         "atomic_int foo, bar = -1; atomic_store(&foo, 0); foo += bar"  \
         $LATOMIC && eval stdatomic_extralibs="\$LATOMIC" && break
